                "nodeCode": "KN-PREFACE-008",
                "locale": "en",
                "title": "Why Reality Is Harder to Understand: Speed Mismatch, Operating Cost, and Reality Grammar",
                "summary": "Pressure does not come only from a world becoming faster. It also comes from systems changing at incompatible speeds and from the attention, time, energy, and maintenance required to keep them operating. Understanding this complexity requires a language of formation, operation, position, and continuity.",
                "href": "/articles/why-reality-is-harder-to-understand-speed-cost-and-reality-grammar",
                "score": 395
              },
              {
                "nodeCode": "KN-B1-P2-007",
                "locale": "en",
                "title": "Why the Same World Produces Different Realities: From Structure and Position to Shared Projection",
                "summary": "People do not encounter a common world through identical entry points. Structure organizes what can connect, function determines what structures do, networks carry influence, and position determines what a system can see. Shared reality emerges when multiple projections become coordinated, stabilized, and repeatedly revised across institutions, history, civilization, and increasingly artificial systems.",
                "href": "/articles/how-structure-position-and-shared-projection-create-different-realities",
                "score": 390
              },
              {
                "nodeCode": "KN-B1-P1-003",
                "locale": "en",
                "title": "Why Does Reality Need Structure?",
                "summary": "Structure is not a fixed shape that exists before Difference. It forms when Constraint selects relations that can be maintained and Feedback helps those relations become durable enough to create Continuity, boundaries, and readable organization.",
                "href": "/articles/structure-forms-from-sustainable-relations",
                "score": 355
              }
            ],
            "fragments": [
              {
                "text": "# Why Reality Is Harder to Understand: Speed Mismatch, Operating Cost, and Reality Grammar",
                "fragmentCode": "FRAGMENT-KN-PREFACE-008-EN-001",
                "digest": "11e05cab3ff2d0413070ba22b3b228fc7effa4c62e57d68d06f8b8da59805ee8"
              },
              {
                "text": "It is common to say that the world is getting faster, but speed alone does not explain why reality can become difficult to carry. A deeper problem appears when different systems operate on clocks that no longer fit together. Technology may change within months. Organizational processes can take years to redesign. Human learning, trust, recovery, and judgment each move at still different rates. When these speeds stop coordinating, pressure is produced by mismatch rather than by speed in isolation.",
                "fragmentCode": "FRAGMENT-KN-PREFACE-008-EN-002",
                "digest": "2ed13e3480778e5b36db89a44c70d5f2c757e773da940cee4cf79a5071ce4cb5"
              }
            ]
